<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Enomoto Takeaki</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1836">1836</a>–<a href="/years/1908">1908</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Enomoto Takeaki was a Japanese admiral of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa shogunate</a> who refused to surrender its fleet in 1868 and sailed north to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hokkaido">Hokkaido</a>. There he was elected president of the Republic of Ezo in 1869 and held out until he surrendered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goryokaku">Goryōkaku</a> after the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hakodate">Hakodate</a>. Pardoned, he later served the Meiji government as a diplomat and minister, negotiating the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-petersburg">Saint Petersburg</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1875.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/enomoto-takeaki.jpg" alt="Enomoto Takeaki" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Enomoto_Takeaki.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
